      "problem": "Solve the equation $x-8 =6.$",
      "worked_solution": "To isolate $x$, we need to perform the *opposite* of subtracting $8$ from $x$, which is *adding* $8$ to $x.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    \t\tx-8 &= 6 \\\n\t\tx-8+8 &= 6+8 \\\n\t\tx+0 &= 14 \\\n\t\tx &= 14\n\t}\n$$",
